# /ai-usage-review — Standalone Adapter

This is a thin adapter for the standalone `ai-usage-review` CLI.

The standalone repo is canonical. GStack should route to it, not reimplement its
collector, evidence schema, coaching logic, or guidance ledger.

## Lane

Use this skill for coaching how the user used AI: prompts, workflow choices,
tool/session metadata, strengths, teaching notes, and feature-fit advice.

Do not use this skill for:

- `/retro` — project productivity, commits, shipping history
- `/review` — code correctness or PR defects
- `/learn` — managing stored learnings
- `/office-hours` — product/startup idea diagnosis
- `/benchmark-models` — comparing model performance

## Resolve CLI

```bash
AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD=""
if [ -n "${AI_USAGE_REVIEW_BIN:-}" ] && [ -x "$AI_USAGE_REVIEW_BIN" ]; then
  AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD="$AI_USAGE_REVIEW_BIN"
elif command -v ai-usage-review >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD="$(command -v ai-usage-review)"
elif [ -n "${AI_USAGE_REVIEW_ROOT:-}" ] && [ -f "$AI_USAGE_REVIEW_ROOT/src/cli.ts" ]; then
  AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD="bun run $AI_USAGE_REVIEW_ROOT/src/cli.ts"
elif [ -f "$HOME/Developer/AI-Research/ai-usage-review/src/cli.ts" ]; then
  AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD="bun run $HOME/Developer/AI-Research/ai-usage-review/src/cli.ts"
else
  echo "AI_USAGE_REVIEW_NOT_FOUND"
fi
echo "AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD: ${AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD:-missing}"
```

If `AI_USAGE_REVIEW_NOT_FOUND`, stop and tell the user to install the standalone
repo or set `AI_USAGE_REVIEW_ROOT=/path/to/ai-usage-review`.

## Writing Standard

Present the output like an engineering lesson:

- start with the strongest observed pattern
- name what the user did well
- explain why a pattern matters
- cite evidence IDs and source links
- give a concrete next-session script
- say what the review could not see

Do not turn the report into a generic scorecard. Do not imply complete desktop
coverage when the standalone CLI reported schema skips or experimental sources.

## Interactive Workflow

1. Ask what the user was trying to accomplish in the reviewed window unless they
   said "no questions" or "just run it".
2. Run the standalone CLI:
   ```bash
   $AI_USAGE_REVIEW_CMD review --project "$(pwd)" --since 21d --no-questions --no-second-opinion
   ```
   Adjust `--project`, `--since`, `--second-opinion`, and
   `--include-experimental-desktop-sources` if the user specified them.
3. Read the printed `report.md` path.
4. Present the teaching summary first: one-line read, strengths, patterns,
   feature-fit advice, next-session script.
5. Ask whether they want to go deeper, run second opinion, skip, next, or end.

## Second Opinion

If the user asks for second opinion, pass `--second-opinion`. The standalone CLI
handles provider selection and validation. Do not run your own separate review
unless the CLI asks you to.
